===Alternative forms===
* [[dirsë]] (Gheg)

===Etymology===
Probably from {{term|djerr|lang=sq}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|ters-||dry|lang=ine-pro}}, cognate to Ancient Greek {{term|τέρσομαι|tr=tersomai|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Sanskrit {{term|तृष्यति|sc=Deva|tr=tṛṣyati|lang=sa}}, {{etyl|ang}} {{term|þurst|lang=ang}} and Latin {{term|terra|lang=la}}. Alternatively from {{etyl|sqj-pro|sq}} {{recons|widertjā|lang=sqj-pro}}, from {{recons|swidertjā|lang=sqj-pro}}, from pre-Albanian {{recons|swidrotyeh₂|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sq}} {{recons|sweyd-|lang=ine-pro}} (compare Greek {{term|ιδρός|tr=idrós|lang=el}}, English {{term|sweat|lang=en}}, Italian {{term|sudore|lang=it}}).

